/// The apps the platform runs, each from the image its CI publishes: a
/// container of the app (and of its worker), its production variables
/// (yours, encrypted in secrets/apps/<app>.sops.env, and the platform's:
/// its database, where telemetry goes), and its deploys. A tag of the app
/// deploys itself (esquadro's deploy blueprint, in the app): its CI signs
/// in to the server with a key that can only deploy that app, which pulls
/// the version, migrates its database, replaces the containers and, if they
/// are not healthy, goes back to the version before. task deploy deploys
/// or rolls back from here.
blueprint apps {
  version "0.1.0"
  for platform
  requires server
  optional postgres, caddy

  /// Variables the platform gives every app, as YAML "KEY: value" lines
  /// indented by two spaces; Jinja sees app, the app's settings.
  slot "apps.env"
}
